<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sanjak of Smederevo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1459–1817</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Pashalik of Belgrade</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sanjak of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smederevo">Smederevo</a>, later known as the Pashalik of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgrade">Belgrade</a>, was an Ottoman province in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> created after the conquest of Smederevo in 1459 and governed from Belgrade after 1521. In 1801 renegade <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/janissaries">janissaries</a>, the dahije, seized power there, and their terror provoked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-serbian-uprising">First Serbian Uprising</a> of 1804. Its territory became the core of the autonomous Principality of Serbia from 1815.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sanjak-of-smederevo.jpg" alt="Sanjak of Smederevo" width="320" height="248" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Belgrade_pashaluk.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
